{"step_index":175,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:52:29Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-31T19:52:29Z sender=ad11b698-02fb-4a11-aa96-f97670e45f28 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=I have generated the requested Python script for Blender that sets up a particle system explosion (like a firework), configures the camera and lighting, and sets the render output to a PNG sequence in `particle_render`.\n\nHowever, as a read-only research subagent, I do not have the `write_to_file` tool. Please use your write tools to save the following code to `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\blender\\particle_sim.py`.\n\n```python\nimport bpy\nimport math\n\n# Clear existing objects\nbpy.ops.wm.read_factory_settings(use_empty=True)\n\n# 1. Create Emitter Object (Ico Sphere)\nbpy.ops.mesh.primitive_ico_sphere_add(subdivisions=3, radius=0.5, location=(0, 0, 5))\nemitter = bpy.context.active_object\nemitter.name = \"FireworkEmitter\"\n\n# 2. Add Particle System\nbpy.ops.object.particle_system_add()\npsys = emitter.particle_systems[0]\npsys.name = \"Explosion\"\n\n# Configure Particle System Settings\npset = psys.settings\npset.count = 3000\npset.frame_start = 10\npset.frame_end = 15\npset.lifetime = 50\npset.lifetime_random = 0.5\npset.emit_from = 'VOLUME'\npset.normal_factor = 25.0 # Explosion force\npset.factor_random = 10.0\npset.gravity_factor = 0.5 # Slight gravity pull downwards over time\n\n# Create a material for particles (Emission)\nmat = bpy.data.materials.new(name=\"ParticleMaterial\")\nmat.use_nodes = True\nnodes = mat.node_tree.nodes\nlinks = mat.node_tree.links\n\n# Clear default nodes\nfor node in nodes:\n    nodes.remove(node)\n\n# Add Emission and Output nodes\nemission = nodes.new(type='ShaderNodeEmission')\nemission.inputs['Color'].default_value = (1.0, 0.4, 0.1, 1.0) # Orange/Red\nemission.inputs['Strength'].default_value = 15.0\n\noutput = nodes.new(type='ShaderNodeOutputMaterial')\nlinks.new(emission.outputs['Emission'], output.inputs['Surface'])\n\n# 3. Create Particle Instance Object\nbpy.ops.mesh.primitive_uv_sphere_add(radius=0.1, location=(10, 10, 10))\nparticle_obj = bpy.context.active_object\nparticle_obj.name = \"ParticleObject\"\n\nif len(particle_obj.data.materials) == 0:\n    particle_obj.data.materials.append(mat)\nelse:\n    particle_obj.data.materials[0] = mat\n\n# Hide instance object from render and viewport\nparticle_obj.hide_render = True\nparticle_obj.hide_set(True)\n\n# Apply Particle Render Settings\npset.render_type = 'OBJECT'\npset.instance_object = particle_obj\npset.particle_size = 0.2\npset.size_random = 0.6\nemitter.show_instancer_for_render = False\n\n# 4. Setup Camera\nbpy.ops.object.camera_add(location=(0, -25, 5), rotation=(math.radians(90), 0, 0))\ncamera = bpy.context.active_object\nbpy.context.scene.camera = camera\n\n# 5. Setup Lighting\nbpy.ops.object.light_add(type='AREA', location=(0, -10, 10))\nlight = bpy.context.active_object\nlight.data.energy = 5000\nlight.data.color = (0.8, 0.9, 1.0)\nlight.data.shape = 'RECTANGLE'\nlight.data.size = 10\n\n# Darken world background for better firework visibility\nworld = bpy.context.scene.world\nif world and world.node_tree:\n    bg_node = world.node_tree.nodes.get(\"Background\")\n    if bg_node:\n        bg_node.inputs[0].default_value = (0.01, 0.01, 0.02, 1.0) # Dark background\n\n# 6. Render Settings\nscene = bpy.context.scene\nscene.render.engine = 'CYCLES' # CYCLES handles emission lighting well\nscene.render.image_settings.file_format = 'PNG'\n\n# Set render output to PNG sequence in 'particle_render' relative to the blend file\nscene.render.filepath = \"//particle_render/\"\nscene.frame_start = 1\nscene.frame_end = 100\n\nprint(\"Particle system explosion setup complete.\")\n```\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
